AEGIS Debian packaging notes
===========================

This package intentionally does not auto-enable `aegis-server.service` or
`aegis-client.service` on install.

Why:
- AEGIS has explicit `server` and `client` roles.
- Operators must choose which role belongs on which host.
- The Linux-first client runtime can require privileged networking setup.

Recommended operator flow:
1. Install the package.
2. Review `/etc/default/aegis-server` or `/etc/default/aegis-client`.
3. Prepare config and certificates under `/etc/aegis/...`.
4. Explicitly enable the needed unit with `systemctl enable --now ...`.

The preset policy lives in `/usr/lib/systemd/system-preset/90-aegis.preset`.
